module

public import Mathlib.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Presheaf.ColimitFunctor
public import Mathlib.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Presheaf.Pushforward
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Cech.PairApproximation
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Cech.PairCategory

/-!
# The index category of Stacks 099D's colimit, and its colimit

Step 2 of the proof of Stacks 099D passes from presented pairs to an arbitrary pair `(A, I)`
with `I` finitely generated by the filtered colimit

`K(A, I) = colim K(A₀, I₀)`,

the colimit being taken over the category of ring maps `φ : A₀ →+* A` out of a presented pair
`(A₀, I₀)` with `Ideal.map φ I₀ = I`, the morphisms being morphisms of pairs commuting with the
maps to `A`. The source asserts that this index category is filtered and that `colim A₀ = A`,
and omits both proofs. This file supplies them, and feeds the second into Mathlib's
`PresheafOfModules.colimitFunctor` to get the colimit of a pair-module as an `A`-module.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver A I` — an object of the index category: a presented pair
  `P : Stacks.PairSite.Pair` together with `φ : P.ring →+* A` satisfying
  `Ideal.map φ P.ideal = I`. Its `CategoryTheory.Category` instance is the index category.
* `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.proj` — the projection to the category of pairs.
* `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.approx` — the approximation of `(A, I)` underlying an object: the
  image subalgebra with the image ideal. This is the bridge to
  `Stacks.PairApproximation.PairApprox`, where the combinatorial step is already proved.
* `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.Presents` — a presentation of an approximation by an object of the
  index category with injective structure map.
* `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.ringCocone` — the cocone on the diagram of rings
  `o ↦ (o.pair).ring` with vertex `A` given by the structure maps.
* `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.transport` — functoriality: a ring map `φ : A →+* B` with
  `J = Ideal.map φ I` induces a functor between the index categories, by composing the structure
  map with `φ`.
* `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.colimitFunctor` — the colimit functor `PairModule ⥤ ModuleCat A`
  sending a presheaf of modules on the site of pairs to the colimit, over the index category, of
  its values. Its target is `ModuleCat A` because `A` is the colimit of the rings.
* `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.colimitComplexFunctor` — the same, degreewise on cochain complexes:
  a complex of pair-modules has a colimit which is a complex of `A`-modules.
* `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.germ` — the structure map of that colimit cocone at an object of
  the index category, with `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.germ_restriction` the cocone condition.

## Main results

* `Stacks.PairSite.Pair.range_eval` — the image of `Stacks.PairSite.Pair.eval` is the
  `ℤ`-subalgebra generated by the chosen elements. This is what presents a finite-type
  `ℤ`-subalgebra of `A` by a polynomial ring.
* `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.exists_pairOver_approx_eq` — **every approximation of `(A, I)` is
  the image of an object of the index category whose structure map is injective.** This is the
  cofinality statement that transports the work done on the poset of approximations to the index
  category.
* `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.exists_hom` — **the factorization property**: an object maps to any
  object whose structure map is injective and whose approximation dominates its own.
* `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.instIsFilteredOrEmpty` and
  `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.isFiltered` — **the index category is filtered** when `I` is
  finitely generated. This is the proof the source omits. The index category is not a poset:
  two objects can have the same image subalgebra with different presentations, and two parallel
  morphisms between fixed objects need not be equal, so the coequalizing condition has content.
  It is settled by mapping the target to an object with injective structure map.
* `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.existsUnique_ringHom`,
  `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.isColimit_ringCocone` and
  `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.isColimit_indexRingCocone` — **`A = colim A₀`**, as a universal
  property of ring maps and as a colimit in `RingCat`, over the index category and over its
  double opposite (which is the form `PresheafOfModules` consumes).
* `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.transport_comp`, `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.transport_id` — the
  transports compose on the nose, and `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.desc_transportCocone` — the map
  induced on the colimits by `φ : A →+* B` is `φ` itself.

## Implementation notes

The index category is a bespoke structure rather than a full subcategory of
`CategoryTheory.CostructuredArrow Stacks.PairSite.ringFunctor (RingCat.of A)`. The comma
category does give the right objects and morphisms — its morphisms are exactly morphisms of
pairs commuting with the maps to `A`, by `CategoryTheory.CostructuredArrow.w` — but its type of
objects lands in `Type (u + 1)`, because `CategoryTheory.CostructuredArrow` is a
`CategoryTheory.Comma` category whose second index is `CategoryTheory.Discrete PUnit.{u + 1}`.
`PresheafOfModules.colimitFunctor` requires its site to be `CategoryTheory.LocallySmall.{u}`
and `CategoryTheory.InitiallySmall.{u}`, which for a structure in `Type u` is immediate and for
the comma category would need a detour through `CategoryTheory.EssentiallySmall`. The
projection `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.proj` and the field `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.hom` record
the same data the comma category would.

Filteredness is proved by transport from `Stacks.PairApproximation.PairApprox`, whose
`Stacks.PairApproximation.PairApprox.exists_ge_ge` carries out the coefficient-adjunction
argument. What this file adds is the comparison between the poset of approximations and the
index category, in both directions: `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.approx` goes one way, and
`Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.exists_pairOver_approx_eq` the other. The second needs the
presentation of a finite-type `ℤ`-subalgebra of `A` by a polynomial ring, which is
`Stacks.PairSite.Pair.range_eval` together with `Stacks.PairSite.Pair.ofEval`.

The colimit of the modules is Mathlib's `PresheafOfModules.colimitFunctor`, which consumes
exactly the datum produced here — a colimit cocone for a presheaf of rings on a cofiltered
category — and produces modules over the vertex of that cocone. No new colimit construction is
needed: the pullback of a pair-module along the projection is
`PresheafOfModules.pushforward₀`, and the `A`-module structure on the colimit is the one
Mathlib builds out of the colimit cocone of rings.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 099D](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/099D)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 00QY](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00QY)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Stacks.PairApproximation

universe u

namespace Stacks.PairSite

variable {A B D : Type u} [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [CommRing D]
variable {I : Ideal A} {J : Ideal B} {L : Ideal D}

/-! ### Generalities -/

private theorem map_algHom_eq {R S T : Type*} [CommSemiring R] [Semiring S] [Semiring T]
    [Algebra R S] [Algebra R T] (f : S →ₐ[R] T) (K : Ideal S) :
    K.map f = K.map f.toRingHom := rfl

private theorem map_span_range {R S : Type u} [CommRing R] [CommRing S] (f : R →+* S)
    {ι : Type*} (v : ι → R) :
    (Ideal.span (Set.range v)).map f = Ideal.span (Set.range fun i => f (v i)) := by
  rw [Ideal.map_span, ← Set.range_comp]
  rfl

/-! ### Presenting a finite-type `ℤ`-subalgebra by a polynomial ring

`Pair.ofEval x y` presents a pair whose ring injects into `A` with image the `ℤ`-subalgebra
generated by the `x i`. The identification of that image is the lemma below, and it is what
makes every finite-type `ℤ`-subalgebra of `A` the image of a presented pair. -/

namespace Pair

variable {R : Type u} [CommRing R]

private theorem range_eval_subset_closure {n : ℕ} (x : Fin n → R) :
    Set.range (eval x) ⊆ (Subring.closure (Set.range x) : Set R) := by
  rintro _ ⟨p, rfl⟩
  induction p using MvPolynomial.induction_on with
  | C a =>
    rw [show eval x (MvPolynomial.C a) = ((ULift.ringEquiv a : ℤ) : R) by simp [eval]]
    exact intCast_mem _ _
  | add p q hp hq =>
    rw [map_add]
    exact add_mem hp hq
  | mul_X p i hp =>
    rw [map_mul, eval_X]
    exact mul_mem hp (Subring.subset_closure ⟨i, rfl⟩)

private theorem closure_subset_range_eval {n : ℕ} (x : Fin n → R) :
    (Subring.closure (Set.range x) : Set R) ⊆ Set.range (eval x) := by
  have h : Subring.closure (Set.range x) ≤ (eval x).range := by
    rw [Subring.closure_le]
    rintro _ ⟨i, rfl⟩
    exact ⟨MvPolynomial.X i, eval_X x i⟩
  intro a ha
  obtain ⟨p, hp⟩ := h ha
  exact ⟨p, hp⟩

/-- **The image of `Pair.eval x` is the `ℤ`-subalgebra generated by the `x i`.** Together with
`Stacks.PairSite.Pair.ofEval` this presents every finite-type `ℤ`-subalgebra of a ring as the
image of the ring of a presented pair. -/
theorem range_eval {n : ℕ} (x : Fin n → R) :
    Set.range (eval x) = (Algebra.adjoin ℤ (Set.range x) : Set R) := by
  rw [Algebra.adjoin_int]
  exact Set.Subset.antisymm (range_eval_subset_closure x) (closure_subset_range_eval x)

/-- The ring map out of the ring of `Pair.ofEval x y` has the same image as `Pair.eval x`: the
relations imposed are exactly the kernel. -/
theorem range_ofEvalHom {n : ℕ} (x : Fin n → R) :
    Set.range (ofEvalHom x) = Set.range (eval x) := by
  conv_rhs => rw [← ofEvalHom_comp_mk x]
  rw [RingHom.coe_comp, Set.range_comp, Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective.range_eq, Set.image_univ]

end Pair

/-! ### The index category -/

/-- **An object of the index category of Stacks 099D's colimit.** A presented pair `P` together
with a ring map `φ : P.ring →+* A` carrying the ideal of `P` onto `I`. -/
structure PairOver (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (I : Ideal A) : Type u where
  /-- The presented pair. -/
  pair : Pair.{u}
  /-- The structure map to `A`. -/
  hom : pair.ring →+* A
  /-- The structure map carries the ideal of the pair onto `I`. -/
  map_ideal : Ideal.map hom pair.ideal = I

namespace PairOver

/-- **A morphism of the index category**: a morphism of pairs commuting with the structure maps
to `A`. -/
structure Hom (X Y : PairOver A I) where
  /-- The underlying morphism of pairs. -/
  toHom : X.pair ⟶ Y.pair
  /-- Commutation with the structure maps. -/
  w : Y.hom.comp toHom.toRingHom = X.hom

/-- A morphism of the index category is determined by its underlying morphism of pairs. -/
theorem Hom.ext' {X Y : PairOver A I} :
    ∀ {f g : Hom X Y}, f.toHom = g.toHom → f = g
  | ⟨_, _⟩, ⟨_, _⟩, rfl => rfl

/-- **The index category of Stacks 099D's colimit.** It is a small category: `PairOver A I` and
its morphisms both live in `Type u`. -/
instance : Category.{u, u} (PairOver A I) where
  Hom X Y := PairOver.Hom X Y
  id X := ⟨𝟙 X.pair, RingHom.comp_id X.hom⟩
  comp {X Y Z} f g := ⟨f.toHom ≫ g.toHom, by
    rw [Pair.comp_toRingHom, ← RingHom.comp_assoc, g.w, f.w]⟩
  id_comp f := Hom.ext' (Category.id_comp f.toHom)
  comp_id f := Hom.ext' (Category.comp_id f.toHom)
  assoc f g h := Hom.ext' (Category.assoc f.toHom g.toHom h.toHom)

/-- The underlying morphism of pairs of an identity is the identity. -/
@[simp]
theorem id_toHom (X : PairOver A I) : Hom.toHom (𝟙 X) = 𝟙 X.pair := rfl

/-- The underlying morphism of pairs of a composite is the composite of the underlying
morphisms. -/
@[simp]
theorem comp_toHom {X Y Z : PairOver A I} (f : X ⟶ Y) (g : Y ⟶ Z) :
    (f ≫ g).toHom = f.toHom ≫ g.toHom := rfl

/-- A morphism `f : X ⟶ Y` commutes with the structure maps, evaluated at an element. -/
@[simp]
theorem hom_apply_toRingHom {X Y : PairOver A I} (f : X ⟶ Y) (a : X.pair.ring) :
    Y.hom ((Hom.toHom f).toRingHom a) = X.hom a :=
  congrArg (fun φ : X.pair.ring →+* A => φ a) (Hom.w f)

/-- **The projection to the category of pairs.** -/
def proj (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (I : Ideal A) : PairOver A I ⥤ Pair.{u} where
  obj X := X.pair
  map f := Hom.toHom f
  map_id _ := rfl
  map_comp _ _ := rfl

/-- The projection sends an object to its underlying pair. -/
@[simp]
theorem proj_obj (X : PairOver A I) : (proj A I).obj X = X.pair := rfl

/-- The projection sends a morphism to its underlying morphism of pairs. -/
@[simp]
theorem proj_map {X Y : PairOver A I} (f : X ⟶ Y) : (proj A I).map f = Hom.toHom f := rfl

/-- The index category is locally small: it is small. -/
instance : LocallySmall.{u} (PairOver A I) := ⟨fun _ _ => inferInstance⟩

/-! ### The approximation underlying an object -/

/-- **The approximation of `(A, I)` underlying an object of the index category**: the image of
the structure map, with the image of the ideal. The image is a `ℤ`-subalgebra of finite type
because the ring of a presented pair is a finite-type `ℤ`-algebra. -/
def approx (X : PairOver A I) : PairApprox A I where
  sub := AlgHom.range X.hom.toIntAlgHom
  sub_fg := by
    rw [← Algebra.map_top]
    exact (Algebra.FiniteType.out : (⊤ : Subalgebra ℤ X.pair.ring).FG).map _
  ideal := Ideal.map (AlgHom.rangeRestrict X.hom.toIntAlgHom) X.pair.ideal
  map_ideal := by
    rw [Ideal.map_mapₐ, AlgHom.val_comp_rangeRestrict]
    exact X.map_ideal

/-- The subalgebra of the approximation of `X` is the range of the structure map. -/
@[simp]
theorem approx_sub (X : PairOver A I) : (approx X).sub = AlgHom.range X.hom.toIntAlgHom := rfl

/-- As a set, the subalgebra of the approximation of `X` is the range of the structure map. -/
theorem coe_approx_sub (X : PairOver A I) : ((approx X).sub : Set A) = Set.range X.hom := rfl

/-- The range restriction of the structure map, as a ring map onto the approximating
subalgebra. -/
abbrev rangeRestrict (X : PairOver A I) : X.pair.ring →+* (approx X).sub :=
  (AlgHom.rangeRestrict X.hom.toIntAlgHom).toRingHom

/-- The ideal of the approximation of `X` is the image of the ideal of `X.pair` under
`rangeRestrict X`. -/
theorem approx_ideal (X : PairOver A I) :
    (approx X).ideal = Ideal.map (rangeRestrict X) X.pair.ideal := rfl

/-- The value of `rangeRestrict X` at `a`, read in `A`, is the structure map at `a`. -/
@[simp]
theorem coe_rangeRestrict (X : PairOver A I) (a : X.pair.ring) :
    ((rangeRestrict X a : (approx X).sub) : A) = X.hom a := rfl

/-- The range restriction of the structure map is surjective. -/
theorem rangeRestrict_surjective (X : PairOver A I) : Function.Surjective (rangeRestrict X) :=
  AlgHom.rangeRestrict_surjective _

/-! ### Every approximation comes from an object -/

private theorem pairApprox_eq_of_sub_eq {p q : PairApprox A I} (hsub : p.sub = q.sub)
    (hid : q.ideal = p.ideal.map (Subalgebra.inclusion hsub.le)) : p = q := by
  refine le_antisymm (PairApprox.le_def.2 ⟨hsub.le, hid⟩) (PairApprox.le_def.2 ⟨hsub.ge, ?_⟩)
  rw [hid, Ideal.map_mapₐ,
    show (Subalgebra.inclusion hsub.ge).comp (Subalgebra.inclusion hsub.le) =
      AlgHom.id ℤ p.sub from AlgHom.ext fun _ => Subtype.ext rfl, Ideal.map_idₐ]

private theorem exists_fin_adjoin (S : Subalgebra ℤ A) (hS : S.FG) :
    ∃ (n : ℕ) (x : Fin n → A), Algebra.adjoin ℤ (Set.range x) = S := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨t, ht⟩ := hS
  refine ⟨t.card, fun i => ((t.equivFin.symm i : {a // a ∈ t}) : A), ?_⟩
  rw [show (Set.range fun i => ((t.equivFin.symm i : {a // a ∈ t}) : A)) = (t : Set A) from ?_]
  · exact ht
  · rw [show (fun i => ((t.equivFin.symm i : {a // a ∈ t}) : A)) =
      (Subtype.val ∘ t.equivFin.symm) from rfl, Set.range_comp,
      t.equivFin.symm.range_eq_univ, Set.image_univ, Subtype.range_coe_subtype]
    exact Finset.setOfPred_mem

/-- **Every approximation of `(A, I)` is the image of an object of the index category, by an
injective structure map.** This is the cofinality statement which transports the work done on
the poset `Stacks.PairApproximation.PairApprox A I` to the index category: present the
approximating subalgebra by a polynomial ring in finitely many of its generators, and the
approximating ideal by finitely many polynomials in those variables. -/
theorem exists_pairOver_approx_eq (r : PairApprox A I) :
    ∃ X : PairOver A I, approx X = r ∧ Function.Injective X.hom := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨n, x, hx⟩ := exists_fin_adjoin r.sub r.sub_fg
  obtain ⟨m, g, hg⟩ := r.exists_fin_span
  have hmem : ∀ j, ((g j : r.sub) : A) ∈ Set.range (Pair.eval x) := fun j => by
    rw [Pair.range_eval, hx]
    exact (g j).2
  choose y hy using hmem
  have hrange : Set.range (Pair.ofEvalHom x) = (r.sub : Set A) := by
    rw [Pair.range_ofEvalHom, Pair.range_eval, hx]
  have hmapideal : Ideal.map (Pair.ofEvalHom x) (Pair.ofEval x y).ideal = I := by
    rw [Pair.map_ideal_ofEvalHom, show (fun j => Pair.eval x (y j)) =
      (fun j => ((g j : r.sub) : A)) from funext hy]
    exact r.span_range_val hg
  refine ⟨⟨Pair.ofEval x y, Pair.ofEvalHom x, hmapideal⟩, ?_, Pair.ofEvalHom_injective x⟩
  set X : PairOver A I := ⟨Pair.ofEval x y, Pair.ofEvalHom x, hmapideal⟩ with hX
  have hsub : (approx X).sub = r.sub := SetLike.ext' hrange
  set Φ : X.pair.ring →+* r.sub :=
    (Subalgebra.inclusion hsub.le).toRingHom.comp (rangeRestrict X) with hΦ
  have step1 : (approx X).ideal.map (Subalgebra.inclusion hsub.le) =
      Ideal.map Φ X.pair.ideal :=
    Ideal.map_map (rangeRestrict X) (Subalgebra.inclusion hsub.le).toRingHom
  have step2 : Ideal.map Φ X.pair.ideal = Ideal.span (Set.range fun j =>
      Φ (Ideal.Quotient.mk (RingHom.ker (Pair.eval x)) (y j))) :=
    (Ideal.map_map (Ideal.Quotient.mk (RingHom.ker (Pair.eval x))) Φ).trans
      (map_span_range _ _)
  have key : ∀ j, Φ (Ideal.Quotient.mk (RingHom.ker (Pair.eval x)) (y j)) = g j := fun j =>
    Subtype.ext (hy j)
  refine pairApprox_eq_of_sub_eq hsub ?_
  rw [step1, step2, congrArg Ideal.span (congrArg Set.range (funext key)), hg]

/-! ### The factorization property -/

/-- **The factorization property of the index category.** If the approximation of `X` is
dominated by the approximation of `Y` and the structure map of `Y` is injective, then there is a
morphism `X ⟶ Y`. Injectivity of the structure map of `Y` is what makes the underlying ring map
exist; the domination is what makes it carry the ideal of `X` *onto* the ideal of `Y`, which an
arbitrary factorization of ring maps would not. -/
theorem exists_hom {X Y : PairOver A I} (hY : Function.Injective Y.hom)
    (h : approx X ≤ approx Y) : Nonempty (X ⟶ Y) := by
  obtain ⟨hs, he⟩ := PairApprox.le_def.1 h
  have hinj : Function.Injective (rangeRestrict Y) := fun a b hab =>
    hY (congrArg (fun z : (approx Y).sub => (z : A)) hab)
  let e : Y.pair.ring ≃+* (approx Y).sub :=
    RingEquiv.ofBijective (rangeRestrict Y) ⟨hinj, rangeRestrict_surjective Y⟩
  let incl : (approx X).sub →+* (approx Y).sub := (Subalgebra.inclusion hs).toRingHom
  let f : X.pair.ring →+* Y.pair.ring :=
    ((e.symm : (approx Y).sub →+* Y.pair.ring).comp incl).comp (rangeRestrict X)
  have hsymm : ∀ z : (approx Y).sub, Y.hom (e.symm z) = (z : A) := fun z =>
    congrArg (fun w : (approx Y).sub => (w : A)) (e.apply_symm_apply z)
  have hw : Y.hom.comp f = X.hom := RingHom.ext fun a => by
    show Y.hom (e.symm (incl (rangeRestrict X a))) = X.hom a
    rw [hsymm]
    rfl
  have hcancel : (e.symm : (approx Y).sub →+* Y.pair.ring).comp (rangeRestrict Y) =
      RingHom.id Y.pair.ring := RingHom.ext fun a =>
    e.symm_apply_apply a
  have hideal : Y.pair.ideal = Ideal.map f X.pair.ideal := by
    rw [show Ideal.map f X.pair.ideal =
      Ideal.map (e.symm : (approx Y).sub →+* Y.pair.ring)
        (Ideal.map incl (Ideal.map (rangeRestrict X) X.pair.ideal)) from by
          rw [Ideal.map_map, Ideal.map_map],
      ← approx_ideal X, show Ideal.map incl (approx X).ideal =
        Ideal.map (Subalgebra.inclusion hs) (approx X).ideal from rfl, ← he, approx_ideal Y,
      Ideal.map_map, hcancel, Ideal.map_id]
  exact ⟨⟨⟨f, hideal⟩, hw⟩⟩

/-! ### Filteredness -/

/-- **The index category of Stacks 099D's colimit satisfies the two cocone conditions of a
filtered category.** Two objects are dominated by a third: pass to the approximations, dominate
them by `Stacks.PairApproximation.PairApprox.exists_ge_ge`, and present the dominating
approximation. Two parallel morphisms are coequalized: map the target to an object with
injective structure map, over which the two morphisms become equal because they already agree
after composing with that injective structure map. -/
instance instIsFilteredOrEmpty : IsFilteredOrEmpty (PairOver A I) where
  cocone_objs X Y := by
    obtain ⟨r, h₁, h₂⟩ := PairApprox.exists_ge_ge (approx X) (approx Y)
    obtain ⟨Z, hZ, hZinj⟩ := exists_pairOver_approx_eq r
    obtain ⟨f⟩ := exists_hom hZinj (hZ ▸ h₁ : approx X ≤ approx Z)
    obtain ⟨g⟩ := exists_hom hZinj (hZ ▸ h₂ : approx Y ≤ approx Z)
    exact ⟨Z, f, g, trivial⟩
  cocone_maps {X Y} f g := by
    obtain ⟨Z, hZ, hZinj⟩ := exists_pairOver_approx_eq (approx Y)
    obtain ⟨h⟩ := exists_hom hZinj (le_of_eq hZ.symm)
    refine ⟨Z, h, Hom.ext' (Pair.Hom.ext' (RingHom.ext fun a => hZinj ?_))⟩
    change Z.hom ((Hom.toHom h).toRingHom ((Hom.toHom f).toRingHom a)) =
      Z.hom ((Hom.toHom h).toRingHom ((Hom.toHom g).toRingHom a))
    rw [hom_apply_toRingHom h, hom_apply_toRingHom h, hom_apply_toRingHom f,
      hom_apply_toRingHom g]

/-- The index category is nonempty as soon as `I` is finitely generated. -/
theorem nonempty (hI : I.FG) : Nonempty (PairOver A I) := by
  obtain ⟨r⟩ := PairApprox.nonempty (I := I) hI
  obtain ⟨X, -, -⟩ := exists_pairOver_approx_eq r
  exact ⟨X⟩

/-- **The index category of Stacks 099D's colimit is filtered.** This is the assertion the
source makes and leaves unproved. -/
theorem isFiltered (hI : I.FG) : IsFiltered (PairOver A I) :=
  have := nonempty (I := I) hI
  { toIsFilteredOrEmpty := instIsFilteredOrEmpty }

/-! ### Presentations of an approximation -/

/-- **A presentation of an approximation of `(A, I)`**: an object of the index category whose
structure map is injective and whose underlying approximation is the given one. -/
structure Presents (r : PairApprox A I) : Type u where
  /-- The presenting object. -/
  obj : PairOver A I
  /-- Its approximation is `r`. -/
  approx_eq : approx obj = r
  /-- Its structure map is injective. -/
  inj : Function.Injective obj.hom

/-- Every approximation has a presentation: this is
`Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.exists_pairOver_approx_eq`, packaged. -/
theorem exists_presents (r : PairApprox A I) : Nonempty (Presents r) := by
  obtain ⟨X, h₁, h₂⟩ := exists_pairOver_approx_eq r
  exact ⟨⟨X, h₁, h₂⟩⟩

namespace Presents

variable {r : PairApprox A I} (p : Presents r)

/-- The structure map of a presentation, read as a map onto the approximating subalgebra. -/
def toSub : p.obj.pair.ring →+* r.sub :=
  (Subalgebra.inclusion (le_of_eq (congrArg PairApprox.sub p.approx_eq))).toRingHom.comp
    (rangeRestrict p.obj)

/-- The value of `p.toSub` at `a`, read in `A`, is the structure map at `a`. -/
@[simp]
theorem coe_toSub (a : p.obj.pair.ring) : ((p.toSub a : r.sub) : A) = p.obj.hom a := rfl

/-- The structure map of a presentation is a bijection onto the approximating subalgebra. -/
theorem toSub_bijective : Function.Bijective p.toSub := by
  refine ⟨fun a b hab => p.inj (congrArg (fun z : r.sub => (z : A)) hab), fun z => ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ : (z : A) ∈ Set.range p.obj.hom := by
    rw [← coe_approx_sub, p.approx_eq]
    exact z.2
  exact ⟨a, Subtype.ext ha⟩

/-- The isomorphism between the ring of a presentation and the approximating subalgebra. -/
def equiv : p.obj.pair.ring ≃+* r.sub := RingEquiv.ofBijective p.toSub p.toSub_bijective

/-- The structure map sends `p.equiv.symm z` to `z`, read in `A`. -/
@[simp]
theorem hom_equiv_symm (z : r.sub) : p.obj.hom (p.equiv.symm z) = (z : A) :=
  congrArg (fun w : r.sub => (w : A)) (p.equiv.apply_symm_apply z)

end Presents

/-! ### `A = colim A₀` -/

/-- **`A = colim A₀`, as a universal property.** A family of ring maps out of the rings of the
objects of the index category, compatible with the morphisms, extends uniquely to a ring map out
of `A`. This is the second assertion of Step 2 of Stacks 099D's proof. -/
theorem existsUnique_ringHom (hI : I.FG) {T : Type*} [Ring T]
    (F : ∀ X : PairOver A I, X.pair.ring →+* T)
    (hF : ∀ {X Y : PairOver A I} (f : X ⟶ Y), (F Y).comp (Hom.toHom f).toRingHom = F X) :
    ∃! G : A →+* T, ∀ X : PairOver A I, G.comp X.hom = F X := by
  classical
  let pres : ∀ r : PairApprox A I, Presents r := fun r => (exists_presents r).some
  let G₀ : ∀ r : PairApprox A I, r.sub →+* T := fun r =>
    (F (pres r).obj).comp (pres r).equiv.symm.toRingHom
  have key : ∀ (r : PairApprox A I) (X : PairOver A I), approx X ≤ r → ∀ (a : X.pair.ring)
      (z : r.sub), (z : A) = X.hom a → G₀ r z = F X a := by
    intro r X hle a z hz
    obtain ⟨θ⟩ := exists_hom (pres r).inj (hle.trans (pres r).approx_eq.ge)
    show F (pres r).obj ((pres r).equiv.symm z) = F X a
    rw [(pres r).inj (((pres r).hom_equiv_symm z).trans
      (hz.trans (hom_apply_toRingHom θ a).symm)), ← hF θ]
    rfl
  have hlift : ∀ (p : PairApprox A I) (x : p.sub), ∃ a, (x : A) = (pres p).obj.hom a ∧
      G₀ p x = F (pres p).obj a := by
    intro p x
    obtain ⟨a, rfl⟩ := (pres p).toSub_bijective.2 x
    exact ⟨a, rfl, key p _ (pres p).approx_eq.le a _ rfl⟩
  have hcompat : ∀ {p q : PairApprox A I} (h : p ≤ q) (x : p.sub),
      G₀ q (Subalgebra.inclusion (PairApprox.sub_le_sub h) x) = G₀ p x := by
    intro p q h x
    obtain ⟨a, hxa, hG⟩ := hlift p x
    rw [key q (pres p).obj ((pres p).approx_eq.le.trans h) a _ hxa, hG]
  obtain ⟨G, hGval, hGuniq⟩ := PairApprox.existsUnique_ringHom (I := I) hI G₀ hcompat
  refine ⟨G, fun X => RingHom.ext fun a => ?_, fun G' hG' => ?_⟩
  · exact (hGval (approx X) ⟨X.hom a, a, rfl⟩).trans (key _ X le_rfl a _ rfl)
  · refine hGuniq G' fun p x => ?_
    obtain ⟨a, hxa, hG⟩ := hlift p x
    rw [hxa, hG, ← hG' (pres p).obj]
    rfl

/-- The diagram of rings over the index category, `o ↦ (o.pair).ring`. -/
abbrev ringDiagram (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (I : Ideal A) : PairOver A I ⥤ RingCat.{u} :=
  proj A I ⋙ ringFunctor.{u}

/-- **The cocone on the diagram of rings with vertex `A`** given by the structure maps. -/
def ringCocone (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (I : Ideal A) : Cocone (ringDiagram A I) where
  pt := RingCat.of A
  ι :=
    { app := fun X => RingCat.ofHom X.hom
      naturality := fun X Y f => by
        refine RingCat.hom_ext (RingHom.ext fun a => ?_)
        exact hom_apply_toRingHom f a }

/-- The vertex of `ringCocone A I` is `A`. -/
@[simp]
theorem ringCocone_pt : (ringCocone A I).pt = RingCat.of A := rfl

/-- The leg of `ringCocone A I` at `X` is the structure map of `X`. -/
@[simp]
theorem ringCocone_ι_app (X : PairOver A I) :
    (ringCocone A I).ι.app X = RingCat.ofHom X.hom := rfl

/-- **`A = colim A₀`, as a colimit in `RingCat`.** -/
def isColimit_ringCocone (hI : I.FG) : IsColimit (ringCocone A I) := by
  refine IsColimit.ofExistsUnique fun s => ?_
  obtain ⟨G, hG, hGuniq⟩ := existsUnique_ringHom (T := s.pt.carrier) hI
    (fun X => (s.ι.app X).hom) (fun {X Y} f => congrArg RingCat.Hom.hom (s.w f))
  exact ⟨RingCat.ofHom G, fun X => RingCat.hom_ext (hG X),
    fun m hm => RingCat.hom_ext (hGuniq m.hom fun X => congrArg RingCat.Hom.hom (hm X))⟩

/-! ### The colimit of a pair-module -/

/-- The presheaf of rings on the index site: the structure presheaf of rings on pairs, pulled
back along the projection. -/
abbrev indexRings (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (I : Ideal A) :
    (PairOver A I)ᵒᵖᵒᵖ ⥤ RingCat.{u} :=
  (proj A I).op.op ⋙ structureRings.{u}

/-- The cocone of `Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.ringCocone`, read over the double opposite of the
index category. -/
def indexRingCocone (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (I : Ideal A) : Cocone (indexRings A I) :=
  (ringCocone A I).whisker (unopUnop (PairOver A I))

/-- The vertex of `indexRingCocone A I` is `A`. -/
@[simp]
theorem indexRingCocone_pt : (indexRingCocone A I).pt = RingCat.of A := rfl

/-- **`A = colim A₀` over the double opposite of the index category.** -/
def isColimit_indexRingCocone (hI : I.FG) : IsColimit (indexRingCocone A I) :=
  (isColimit_ringCocone hI).whiskerEquivalence (opOpEquivalence (PairOver A I))

/-- The index category is initially small, being small. -/
theorem initiallySmall_op : InitiallySmall.{u} ((PairOver A I)ᵒᵖ) :=
  have : EssentiallySmall.{u} ((PairOver A I)ᵒᵖ) := essentiallySmallSelf _
  initiallySmall_of_essentiallySmall _

/-- **The colimit, over the index category, of the values of a pair-module.** It is a module
over `A` because `A` is the colimit of the rings of the pairs
(`Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.isColimit_indexRingCocone`). This is the module-level content of
Step 2 of Stacks 099D's proof; applied degreewise to a complex of pair-modules it is
`Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.colimitComplexFunctor`. -/
def colimitFunctor (hI : I.FG) : PairModule.{u} ⥤ ModuleCat.{u} A :=
  haveI := isFiltered (I := I) hI
  haveI := initiallySmall_op (A := A) (I := I)
  PresheafOfModules.pushforward₀.{u} (proj A I).op structureRings.{u} ⋙
    PresheafOfModules.colimitFunctor (isColimit_indexRingCocone (A := A) (I := I) hI)

/-! ### The colimit of a complex of pair-modules -/

section Additive

variable {C₁ : Type u} [Category.{u} C₁] {C₂ : Type u} [Category.{u} C₂]

/-- Pushforward of presheaves of modules along a functor is additive. -/
instance additive_pushforward₀ (F : C₁ ⥤ C₂) (R : C₂ᵒᵖ ⥤ RingCat.{u}) :
    (PresheafOfModules.pushforward₀.{u} F R).Additive where
  map_add := by intros; rfl

end Additive

/-- The constant presheaf-of-modules functor attached to a cocone on a presheaf of rings is
additive. -/
instance additive_constFunctor {C₁ : Type u} [Category.{u} C₁] {R : C₁ᵒᵖ ⥤ RingCat.{u}}
    (cR : Cocone R) : (PresheafOfModules.constFunctor.{u} cR).Additive where
  map_add := by intros; rfl

/-- The colimit functor on presheaves of modules over a cofiltered, initially small category is
additive, being a left adjoint. -/
instance additive_presheafColimitFunctor {C₁ : Type u} [Category.{u} C₁]
    [LocallySmall.{u} C₁] [IsCofiltered C₁] [InitiallySmall.{u} C₁]
    {R : C₁ᵒᵖ ⥤ RingCat.{u}} {cR : Cocone R} (hcR : IsColimit cR) :
    (PresheafOfModules.colimitFunctor.{u} hcR).Additive :=
  (PresheafOfModules.colimitAdjunction hcR).left_adjoint_additive

/-- The colimit of a pair-module over the index category is additive in the pair-module. -/
instance additive_colimitFunctor (hI : I.FG) : (colimitFunctor hI).Additive :=
  haveI := isFiltered (I := I) hI
  haveI := initiallySmall_op (A := A) (I := I)
  inferInstanceAs ((PresheafOfModules.pushforward₀ (proj A I).op structureRings.{u} ⋙
    PresheafOfModules.colimitFunctor (isColimit_indexRingCocone (A := A) (I := I) hI)).Additive)

/-- **The germ map**: the structure map of the colimit cocone at an object of the index
category. It is the component of the unit of `PresheafOfModules.colimitAdjunction`, so it is
an `X.pair.ring`-linear map from the value of the pair-module at `X.pair` to the colimit, the
latter read as an `X.pair.ring`-module along the structure map of `X`. -/
def germ (hI : I.FG) (M : PairModule.{u}) (X : PairOver A I) :
    M.value X.pair ⟶ (ModuleCat.restrictScalars X.hom).obj ((colimitFunctor hI).obj M) :=
  haveI := isFiltered (I := I) hI
  haveI := initiallySmall_op (A := A) (I := I)
  PresheafOfModules.Hom.app
    ((PresheafOfModules.colimitAdjunction
      (isColimit_indexRingCocone (A := A) (I := I) hI)).unit.app
      ((PresheafOfModules.pushforward₀ (proj A I).op structureRings.{u}).obj M))
    (Opposite.op (Opposite.op X))

/-- **The germ maps are compatible with the restriction maps of the pair-module**: this is the
cocone condition, and it is the naturality of the unit of
`PresheafOfModules.colimitAdjunction`. -/
theorem germ_restriction (hI : I.FG) (M : PairModule.{u}) {X Y : PairOver A I} (f : X ⟶ Y)
    (m : M.value X.pair) :
    germ hI M Y (M.restriction (Hom.toHom f) m) = germ hI M X m := by
  have := isFiltered (I := I) hI
  have := initiallySmall_op (A := A) (I := I)
  refine Eq.trans (PresheafOfModules.naturality_apply
    ((PresheafOfModules.colimitAdjunction
      (isColimit_indexRingCocone (A := A) (I := I) hI)).unit.app
      ((PresheafOfModules.pushforward₀ (proj A I).op structureRings.{u}).obj M))
    (Quiver.Hom.op (Quiver.Hom.op f)) m) ?_
  rfl

/-- **The colimit, over the index category, of a complex of pair-modules**: a complex of
`A`-modules. This is the shape Stacks 099D's `K(A, I)` has, for `I` finitely generated: a
complex of pair-modules is evaluated at each object of the index category and the colimit is
taken, the `A`-module structure coming from `A = colim A₀`. -/
def colimitComplexFunctor (hI : I.FG) :
    CochainComplex PairModule.{u} ℤ ⥤ CochainComplex (ModuleCat.{u} A) ℤ :=
  (colimitFunctor hI).mapHomologicalComplex (ComplexShape.up ℤ)

/-! ### Functoriality in the pair -/

/-- **Functoriality in the pair.** A ring map `φ : A →+* B` with `J = Ideal.map φ I` carries an
object of the index category of `(A, I)` to one of `(B, J)`, by composing the structure map with
`φ`, and does nothing to the morphisms. -/
def transport (φ : A →+* B) (hJ : J = Ideal.map φ I) : PairOver A I ⥤ PairOver B J where
  obj X := ⟨X.pair, φ.comp X.hom, by rw [← Ideal.map_map, X.map_ideal, hJ]⟩
  map {X Y} f :=
    let g : X.pair ⟶ Y.pair := Hom.toHom f
    ⟨g, (RingHom.comp_assoc g.toRingHom Y.hom φ).trans
      (congrArg (RingHom.comp φ) (Hom.w f))⟩
  map_id _ := rfl
  map_comp _ _ := rfl

/-- The transport of an object has the same underlying pair. -/
@[simp]
theorem transport_obj_pair (φ : A →+* B) (hJ : J = Ideal.map φ I) (X : PairOver A I) :
    ((transport φ hJ).obj X).pair = X.pair := rfl

/-- The structure map of the transport of `X` is `φ` composed with the structure map of `X`. -/
@[simp]
theorem transport_obj_hom (φ : A →+* B) (hJ : J = Ideal.map φ I) (X : PairOver A I) :
    ((transport φ hJ).obj X).hom = φ.comp X.hom := rfl

/-- The transport does not move the underlying pair: it commutes with the projection on the
nose. -/
theorem transport_comp_proj (φ : A →+* B) (hJ : J = Ideal.map φ I) :
    transport φ hJ ⋙ proj B J = proj A I := rfl

/-- **The transports compose on the nose.** -/
theorem transport_comp (φ : A →+* B) (ψ : B →+* D) (hJ : J = Ideal.map φ I)
    (hL : L = Ideal.map ψ J) :
    transport φ hJ ⋙ transport ψ hL =
      transport (ψ.comp φ) (by rw [hL, hJ, Ideal.map_map]) := rfl

/-- **The transport along the identity is the identity.** -/
theorem transport_id : transport (RingHom.id A) (Ideal.map_id I).symm = 𝟭 (PairOver A I) := rfl

/-- The cocone on the diagram of rings of `(A, I)` with vertex `B` obtained by composing the
structure maps with `φ`. It is the cocone of `(B, J)` pulled back along
`Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.transport`. -/
def transportCocone (φ : A →+* B) (_hJ : J = Ideal.map φ I) : Cocone (ringDiagram A I) where
  pt := RingCat.of B
  ι :=
    { app := fun X => RingCat.ofHom (φ.comp X.hom)
      naturality := fun X Y f => by
        refine RingCat.hom_ext (RingHom.ext fun a => ?_)
        exact congrArg φ (hom_apply_toRingHom f a) }

/-- **The map induced on the colimits by a ring map is the ring map.** The colimit of the
diagram of rings of `(A, I)` is `A`, that of `(B, J)` is `B`, and the comparison map attached to
`Stacks.PairSite.PairOver.transport` is `φ` itself. -/
theorem desc_transportCocone (hI : I.FG) (φ : A →+* B) (hJ : J = Ideal.map φ I) :
    (isColimit_ringCocone hI).desc (transportCocone φ hJ) = RingCat.ofHom φ :=
  ((isColimit_ringCocone hI).uniq (transportCocone φ hJ) (RingCat.ofHom φ)
    fun _ => RingCat.hom_ext rfl).symm

end PairOver

end Stacks.PairSite

end
